ws2_32: list the default route's address first for the local host name

get_local_ips() (gethostbyname() of the local host name) orders the
addresses by default route, then by metric. An interface was marked as
having the default route only when that route was the first of its
routes in the table; on Haiku the host and network routes come first,
so no interface was marked. And the metric comparison subtracted two
unsigned values, so a loopback metric of ~0 (as on Linux) wrapped and
sorted first. The loopback address then came first, as 127.12.34.56:
Need for Speed: Porsche Unleashed takes the first address and offers
UDP play only if it is not 127.x, and without it every race start
crashed (W11). Mark the interface when any of its routes is a default
route, and compare the metrics without wrapping.

--- a/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
@@ -826,7 +826,7 @@
         return -1;
     if (b->default_route && !a->default_route)
         return 1;
-    return a->metric - b->metric;
+    return (a->metric > b->metric) - (a->metric < b->metric);
 }
 
 /* Returns the list of local IP addresses by going through the network
@@ -885,6 +885,8 @@
             {
                 if (route_addrs[j].metric > ifmetric)
                     route_addrs[j].metric = ifmetric;
+                if (ifdefault && !route_addrs[j].default_route)
+                    route_addrs[j].default_route = ifdefault;
                 exists = TRUE;
             }
         }
